senses.gloss:
अह ind. A particle implying
——(a) praise (पूजा);
——(b) separation;
——(c) resolution, ascertainment, certainty; and translated by ‘surely’,
 ‘certainly’, ‘yes’, ‘well’;
——(d) rejecting;
——(e) sending;
——(f) deviation from custom, impropriety त्वमह ग्रामं गच्छ, त्वमह
 रथेनारण्यं गच्छ Sk. स्वयमह रथेन याति, उपाध्यायं पदातिं गमयति Sk.
——(g) hence, therefore (अथ); शर्वरीं भगवन्नद्य सत्यशील
 तवाश्रमे । उषिताः स्मोऽह वसतिमनुजानातु नो भवान् ॥ Rām. 2. 54. 37.

आहत + .{@-तम्@}
—1 A new cloth or garment.
—2 An old garment.
—3 A nonsensical or meaningless speech, an assertion of impossibility;
 e. g. एष वन्ध्यासुतो याति Subhāṣ.
.━{@Comp.@}: आहतलक्षण

अहम् pron. (Nom. sing. of अस्मद्). I [cf. Zend. azem;
 L. ego; Germ. ich.]
